    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d12">

                <pb facs="0177" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg129"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2114.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1867-12-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 23, 1867.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your dispatch of the 6th of December, No.
                    1489, has been received. I approve of the manner in which you have carried out
                    the <pb facs="0178" n="130" xml:id="pg130"/> instructions in my 2087. At the
                    same time, I observe with regret that Lord Stanley has not found it convenient
                    to indicate any practical way of removing the difficulties thus brought to his
                    notice.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
